        "original_id": "d3e5ee64-d9b1-52fe-a874-c7c8dbcf63cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jeffrey Jey, Maurizio Lobina, Gabry Ponte\n- Organizations: Eiffel 65\n- Products: \"Blue (Da Ba Dee)\", \"Move Your Body\", \"Europop\", \"Un'altra Come Te\", Club Test 01\n\nFacts:\n- Eiffel 65 is an Italian musical group consisting of Jeffrey Jey, Maurizio Lobina, and Gabry Ponte.\n- On 15 January 1999, Eiffel 65 released \"Blue (Da Ba Dee)\" as the lead single from their debut album \"Europop\".\n- \"Blue (Da Ba Dee)\" is a song by Eiffel 65.\n- Eiffel 65 are known mainly for the high-charting singles \"Blue (Da Ba Dee)\" and \"Move Your Body\" and for their 1999 studio album \"Europop\".\n- Club Test 01 includes a re-imagined version of Eiffel 65's earlier hit \"Blue (Da Ba Dee)\", followed by an English version and remix of \"Un'altra Come Te\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
